00:31:33.380 --> 00:31:37.370
is printcolumn feature, which
lets you decide what columns

00:31:37.370 --> 00:31:41.000
you want to print by default
when a user performs kubectl

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:42.200
get on that resource.

00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:45.920
Like, for parts you
see certain columns.

00:31:45.920 --> 00:31:48.010
For your own resource
you want to show--

00:31:48.010 --> 00:31:49.660
you want to
customize the output.

00:31:49.660 --> 00:31:54.350
So this is where you
configure the feature for CRD,

00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:56.870
and controller-tools is
going to take this as input

00:31:56.870 --> 00:31:59.810
and generate the CRD yaml files.

00:31:59.810 --> 00:32:08.060
For example, I can
quickly show the config

00:32:08.060 --> 00:32:11.790
for this API, the CRD.

00:32:11.790 --> 00:32:17.940
So the CRD definition for
SqlDB API that we added is--

00:32:17.940 --> 00:32:21.590
so this has generated, for
example, the name of the CRDs

00:32:21.590 --> 00:32:25.250
here, like the PrinterColumn
spec that I showed you earlier.

00:32:25.250 --> 00:32:27.650
This got generated
in the form of here.

00:32:27.650 --> 00:32:31.160
So it's saying that, OK, show
replica is one of the columns.

00:32:31.160 --> 00:32:35.270
And this is the JSONPath
for extracting that value

00:32:35.270 --> 00:32:36.660
that you want to show.

00:32:36.660 --> 00:32:38.000
So there are other features.

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.910
Like, similarly, if you
want to add more validation,

00:32:40.910 --> 00:32:44.330
you can annotate the
fields in your types.go

00:32:44.330 --> 00:32:47.690
with the open API
specific annotations.

00:32:47.690 --> 00:32:49.910
And the controller
tools are going

00:32:49.910 --> 00:32:52.260
to generate the schema
automatically for you.

00:32:52.260 --> 00:33:00.070
So this way, your code is
in sync with the CRD schema.

00:33:00.070 --> 00:33:03.410
So yeah, that was quick
about the CRD schema.

00:33:03.410 --> 00:33:08.767
And then we can look, just
very briefly, at the controller

